CLINICAL REASONING SUMMARY
The patient experienced a severe, acute psychiatric crisis, explicitly threatening self-harm due to a catastrophic financial deadline tied to incomplete medical documentation. Telephone triage accurately identified the immediate threat to life. Urgent face-to-face evaluation was mandatory to conduct an acute suicide risk assessment, provide immediate emotional de-escalation, and perform the necessary functional review to complete the required documentation. By finalizing the paperwork on-site, the absolute trigger for the suicidal ideation was completely neutralized. Deferring this assessment until the next in-hours period would have resulted in the deadline expiring, plunging the patient into an unmanageable crisis with a high probability of completed suicide.

CLINICIAN CARE PLAN
Clinical Interventions: Conducted extensive psychiatric de-escalation. Performed a targeted functional assessment and completed the required "Certificate of Capacity" and associated bureaucratic forms. Provided a copy to the patient and electronically submitted the forms directly to the insurer. Contracted for safety overnight.
